  While Prediction I and II described new developments and the practi­
cal use of the basic findings made by   Cyril Fagan, A.P. Nelson
Page and Vendei Polich, Prediction III is based solely on my own
research In the Transit and Prenatal Transit System which was discussed
in Prediction i.
  P great help in this respect had been the large number of rectified
Radices, sixteen of which had been used for the most efficient Primary
Directional method (the Topocentric System) and the workings of fixed
stars demonstrated in this book. Some of my aims In astrology are, and ,
have always been, to develop astrological techniques which secure both
                            r
 a) a scientifically correct birth time, and

 b) a comprehensive way to practise prediction.

   The main problem for mo^t astrologers is still the authentication of the
true birth time, not only as to the trustworthiness of a time of birth, but
also by means of astrological systems that allow certainty against chance
to be controlled with a high probability factor of success.
  It has been found In practice that In cases where several birth times are
in question for the same nativity, radical delineations of these different
horoscopes are not adequate to select the true birth time.
(See John Lennon, Prediction ii)
 Whilst the most appropriate rectification method so far, giving scienti­
fically acceptable results within one minute of arc, has been demonstrated
with Primary Directions {Prediction ii}, there are a number of other
astrological systems which permit the verification of a birth time In a
most simple way. (Secondary Progressions and Regressions derived from
Sidereal Solar Returns in Prediction i ; the Ascendant-Lunar Chart
demonstrated tn this book).
  Besides this, the two last-mentioned rectification methods,if used alone,
secure a well-authenticated, approximate birth time with enough accuracy
to guarantee a satisfactory handling of analyses and predictions in all the
recommended methods of Prediction i.
  All these astrological systems are closing the ring for the mutual con­
firmation of a scientifically correct birth time. The aim of every astrolo­
ger should be a perfectly authenticated birth time for his own nativity as
demonstrated In the Radices of Edward Kennedy and Juan Peron, and a
well- authenticated Conception-Horoscope (Prenatal Epoch).
