    It has always been a vei'y (llfflcult task to find an answer to the main
questions in Synastry: What the relationship between two or more people
will be like, whether their psychological and emotional characteristics fit
together, and if their relationship will be durable or not.
     The most primitive form of chart comparisons is the Judgement of
Sun-Sign compatibility. Users’of this method maintain that, for instance, a
man with Sun In Aries could not have a harmonious and long-lasting rela­
tionship with a woman who has the Sun in Cancer or Capricorn as the Sun
of the man squares the woman's 5un.
   Instead, this method mainly recommends partnership between Sun-Signs
which are either In opposition or harmonious aspect to each other. There­
fore a person with Sun In Arles is said to fit best with other persons who
have the Sun In the following Signs ; Gemini, Aquarius (sextile); Leo, Sa­
gittarius (trine) and Libra (opposition).
   This example could be applied In the same way for all the twelve Signs
of the Zodiac. However, this way of classifying partnership not only turns
out to be insignificant but is also refuted by the statistical analysis of
about 250 cases which revealed that there are more long-lasting partner­
ships and friendships where the Suns of the two individuals are in square
to each other than one would ever expect.
   It Is easy to understand that Sun-Sign comparisons have to be rejected
for many other reasons, too .
   Before going Into details it is always essential to analyze the horos­
copes of partners separately. There are people who are more or less pre­
destinated for partnership while others are not. In extreme cases there are
horoscopes that have no tendencies for a long-lasting relationship at all.
   People of this kind have no friends, and they may also remain single for
their whole life and not have much contact with the opposite sex.
  Horoscopes with characteristic Capricorn-tendencies, especially with a
Saturn affliction to Venus (for males) or to Mars (for females) have very
little receptivity for the opposite sex, whether because of extreme shy­
ness or because they are not capable of true love. Sometimes, also, the
circumstances In their early life play an important role.
  The best way for gaining experience in astrological techniques Is the
analysis of the astrologer's own Chart, as he should be well Informed of
the circumstances of the events analysed, and consequently will be able,
with growing experience, to build up a good judgement of planetary
symbolism. On the other hand with this he Is also getting experience In
how to Interpret Radix Horoscopes, a branch of astrology which unfortu­
nately Is often handled with little care, although, there Is no doubt. It
needs years of experience before true results can be achieved.
   In order to help young astrologers in choosing the right astrological
tools without spending a lifetime with fictional astrological methods, and
also to save the precious time of the more talented students who have a
good proportional feeling - time which they have to spend before they find
a successful way to learn and practise astrology - I have made a review of
the most popular, more or less fictional astrological methods. In most
cases these have little or no astronomical background, but a superfluous
number of factors which cannot be controlled.
